(7389572, 1160147, 108069, '<td valign="top">Floating in heavy space, light from the bottom - do you rise or fall back down? This texture, these tones, those lines. This is where memory meets imagination in a photo and it''s a powerful place to be.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1155933" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/105000-109999/108069/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1155933.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/105000-109999/108069/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1155933.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/105000-109999/108069/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1155933.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Floating in heavy space, light from the bottom - do you rise or fall back down? This texture, these tones, those lines. This is where memory meets imagination in a photo and it''s a powerful place to be. ', '2015-07-20 00:07:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(7389574, 1159521, 108069, '<td valign="top">An explosion of activity is coming, but here we are, stuck on the edge, with a boy not quite accustomed to the balance between breathing and drowning. It''s a startling moment, and he''ll smile and relax or come bursting out, and we don''t know which, and -- aside from the beautiful processing, the flecks of white scribbles -- that''s what has me hooked.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1155943" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/105000-109999/108069/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1155943.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/105000-109999/108069/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1155943.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/105000-109999/108069/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1155943.jpg"/></a></td>', 'An explosion of activity is coming, but here we are, stuck on the edge, with a boy not quite accustomed to the balance between breathing and drowning. It''s a startling moment, and he''ll smile and relax or come bursting out, and we don''t know which, and -- aside from the beautiful processing, the flecks of white scribbles -- that''s what has me hooked. ', '2015-07-20 00:17:22.000000', NULL, 1),
